# Nexus memory (this workspace)

This folder is tracked by **Nexus** (central memory). Cursor chats are **not** auto-imported.

When you learn durable facts about this project (decisions, architecture, how-to, bugs fixed, deploy notes):

1. Prefer Nexus MCP tools if available: `memory_search` before answering from guesswork; `memory_write` for lasting facts.
2. If MCP is unavailable, tell the user to run:
   `nexus memory propose -k topic/key "the fact (20+ characters)"`
3. Do not dump entire chat transcripts — store concise, reusable facts.

Project identity is resolved from this git repo (folder `central-memory`). The web app may also show `nexus-default`; durable repo facts belong on the git project.
